# COBRA OS — project rules for Cline

## What this project is
COBRA OS is a **minimal, hardened, red team live OS**: Debian trixie
`minbase` + Parrot OS package repos, a rebranded operator shell
(`shell/cobrashell.sh`, forked from THC's hackshell), and the curated
operator command registry (`shell/cobra-ops.sh` — the retired Textual TUI
ported to bash functions). It is **console-only**: no X server, no display
manager, no GUI packages — tmux is the dashboard. Web access is `links2`
(optionally over system tor via `torify`), gated behind `xint`. The
2026-08-15/16 X11/i3/Terminator + Firefox/Tor Browser layer was tried and
reverted — do not resurrect it. It is built for
**authorized penetration testing only** — always frame offensive tooling
around consented, contracted use.

## Prime directives
1. **Minimalism first.** Every package must be justified. If you add a
   package to `chroot-setup.sh`, it must either (a) map to a cobra-ops
   function, or (b) have a written reason in `BUILD_PLAN.md`. Never suggest
   `parrot-tools-full`, desktop environments, or X11/GUI packages of any
   kind (including GUI browsers) — the console-only line only moves if the
   user explicitly reverses it.
2. **Security by default.** Default-deny firewall stays default-deny.
   Root stays locked. History stays off. Internet-touching shell helpers
   stay gated behind `xint`. Never weaken a hardening default without the
   user explicitly asking.
3. **No telemetry, ever.** No analytics, no phone-home, no remote
   sourcing of scripts. cobrashell must only reference its LOCAL copy at
   `/etc/cobra/cobrashell.sh`.
4. **No secrets in the repo.** The `changeme` operator password is a
   documented scaffold default with forced change on first login — never
   replace it with a "real" hardcoded password; instruct the user instead.

## Coding conventions
- Bash: `#!/usr/bin/env bash`, `set -euo pipefail`, quote expansions,
  `shellcheck`-clean style. Always `bash -n` after editing a script.
- Python: stdlib only, and never a UI layer — the Textual TUI was retired
  (2026-08-15). python3 exists for the tools (sqlmap, `serve`, impacket),
  not for COBRA code.
- Command registry rule: adding a function to `shell/cobra-ops.sh`
  REQUIRES the matching package in `chroot-setup.sh` and a row in
  `BUILD_PLAN.md` §2. Keep the three in sync.
- Console-only rule: scripts, shell configs, and cobra-ops functions must
  never require X11/startx/a display. Web access is `links2` (or
  `torify links2`) — deliberate, operator-summoned, xint-gated.
- Preserve upstream provenance comments in `shell/cobrashell.sh`
  (THC hackshell credit stays).

## Build-system rules
- `PARROT_SUITE` must be verified against https://deb.parrot.sh before
  changing it; never silently bump the codename.
- `build-rootfs.sh` / `chroot-setup.sh` require root and run debootstrap
  + chroot — NEVER execute them without explicit user approval.
- New tool categories go in as a `COBRA_PROFILES` case in
  `chroot-setup.sh`, not into the core package list.
- File layout is fixed: scripts at root, shell configs in `shell/`, plan
  in `BUILD_PLAN.md`. Keep README.md in sync with reality.
